From ea3bc6e773b2f11b94f14a5bc7ba180e5c753a52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dag Sommer <dagaleks@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 15:11:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/26] windows: let the epoll shim cross a thread boundary

`Epoll` holds `entries: Vec<OVERLAPPED_ENTRY>`, and `OVERLAPPED_ENTRY` contains
a raw `*mut OVERLAPPED`, so the derived auto-trait makes `Epoll` `!Send`. Device
code that hands an epoll instance to a worker thread therefore cannot compile:
`virtio::vsock::muxer_thread::MuxerThread::run()` spawns exactly such a thread.

The `!Send` is an artefact, not a real constraint. `iocp` is an
`Arc<CompletionPort>`, already `Send + Sync`. `entries` is private, cleared at
the top of every `wait()`, filled by `GetQueuedCompletionStatusEx` and drained
before that call returns, so it is never observed from two threads; the pointers
it transiently holds are kernel-supplied completion keys and OVERLAPPED
addresses, valid process-wide. Assert `Send` with that reasoning written down.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/utils/src/windows/epoll.rs | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/utils/src/windows/epoll.rs b/src/utils/src/windows/epoll.rs
index d880cf0..b9e26a9 100644
--- a/src/utils/src/windows/epoll.rs
+++ b/src/utils/src/windows/epoll.rs
@@ -214,6 +214,19 @@ pub struct Epoll {
     entries: Vec<OVERLAPPED_ENTRY>,
 }
 
+// SAFETY: `iocp` is an `Arc<CompletionPort>`, which is already `Send + Sync`.
+// `entries` is a private scratch buffer that only ever holds output written by
+// `GetQueuedCompletionStatusEx` inside `wait()`: it is filled and drained
+// within a single call, is never observed across threads, and is cleared at the
+// top of every `wait()`. The raw pointers it transiently contains are kernel-
+// supplied completion keys and OVERLAPPED addresses, both valid process-wide.
+//
+// This is needed because device code moves an `Epoll` into a worker thread --
+// `virtio::vsock::muxer_thread::MuxerThread::run()` is one such caller -- which
+// the derived auto-trait forbids purely because `OVERLAPPED_ENTRY` contains a
+// raw pointer.
+unsafe impl Send for Epoll {}
+
 impl Clone for Epoll {
     fn clone(&self) -> Self {
         Epoll {
-- 
